# listen — a person is overheard, never simply listened to
#
# "Listen to the miller's apprentice" read as the opening of a conversation, which is another verb's
# business. A person who speaks is therefore listened to only while somebody else is there for them
# to be talking with, and the act names both. The brewer shares the Test Hall with the reeve
# (--npc-static pins them there), so the act is offered — as overhearing.
#
# The complement, a speaker alone in a room, is cli/verb/listen/alone.cli.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Hall" --period noon --observe-only "brewer"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy succeed
goal listen
advance 12 180

click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
regions
expect talking with

click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

expect SUCCESS
expect Modus mentis
expect-verb listen
quit
